      "severity": "concern",
      "claim": "The spec's \"Context\" (\"Where the re-run is judged\") and \"Notes for the agent\" sections cite dozens of specific line numbers in saffron/cell/session.py and tests/test_session.py that do not match this file at this base commit. Examples: `_judge` is cited at session.py:2529 (actually 2595); the `if attempt is not None:` guard cited at :2557 (actually 2623); the ownership comment cited at :2555-2556, which at this snapshot is unrelated code in the `elif commits == 0:` / Terminal(\"finished_empty\") branch (the real comment is at 2621-2622); `_judge`'s record_gate_result call cited at :2537-2554 (actually 2614-2620); `_rebut_gates` cited as spanning :3027-3044 and calling `_judge()` at :3031 and emitting at :3034-3041 (actually spans 3093-3110, calls at 3097, emits at 3100-3107); `attempt_event` cited at :687-730 (actually 706-749); `repair_loop`'s `judge(attempt)` call cited at :762, which is mid-docstring prose unrelated to the call (the real call is at line 781); in tests/test_session.py, `_through_rebut` cited at :3935 (actually 4180), the example test near criterion 4 cited near :5106 (actually 5508, def test_the_gate_check_after_the_rebuttal_continues_the_gate_count), the \"emits nothing\" docstring sentence cited at :5180-5184 (actually 5582-5586, inside test_each_attempts_gate_results_carry_their_own_attempt_number), and `_task_outcome` cited at :5800 (actually 6424). By contrast, citations into less-churned files (saffron/phases/rebut.py:716, saffron/watch.py:115, saffron/events.py:252, CONTEXT.md:241-245, saffron/gates/baseline.py:67-89, tests/ontology/test_vocabulary_agrees_with_context.py:22-34, tests/test_events.py:49-60, tests/fixtures/watch-golden.txt:62,70) are exactly correct. This one-directional, growing drift is consistent with the Context/Notes having been drafted against an earlier state of session.py/test_session.py and never rebased onto the stated base commit. The substance described at each wrong location is usually still true elsewhere in the file, so the acceptance criteria (which name functions/tests, not lines) remain buildable, but a cell that edits by the given coordinates (as the spec's own precise citation style invites, e.g. \"rewrite the comment at :2555-2556\") risks editing the wrong code.",
      "criterion": null,
      "file": "saffron/cell/session.py",
      "line": 2555,
      "fixes": null
    },
    {
      "severity": "concern",
      "claim": "Notes for the agent states \"tests/test_events.py:1241-1242 pins `len(FAMILIES) == 70`\", but at this snapshot that assertion reads `assert len(FAMILIES) == 71` (and `len({f.prefix for f in FAMILIES}) == 71`). The docstring on that very test (test_the_table_did_not_quietly_lose_a_row) explains why: \"`SA-0235` moves it again, by one.\" SA-0242 depends on SA-0235, and SA-0235 is exactly the commit this spec's base points at, so the dependency that bumped the count from 70 to 71 is already merged into this snapshot and the spec's Notes never absorbed that. The instruction to edit the existing row in place rather than add a new one still holds regardless of the exact count, so this does not block the build, but it is concrete proof the Context/Notes predate the spec's own declared dependency and were not rebased onto the stated base commit — the same root cause as the pervasive line-number drift.",
